#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:34
msgid "Getting the firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:36
msgid ""
"Download the desired MicroPython firmware version for the PSOC™ Edge "
"board from the `MicroPython download page "
"<https://micropython.org/download/>`_. The downloaded file is a ``.zip`` "
"package containing the firmware binary and the necessary files for "
"flashing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:40
msgid "Flashing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:42
msgid ""
"To flash the firmware, use the ``from-package`` command. Specify the "
"board using the ``--board`` flag and the path to the downloaded ``.zip`` "
"package using the ``--zip-package`` flag, as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:46
msgid ""
"$ python mp-ifx-flash.py from-package --board KIT_PSE84_AI --zip-package "
"pathtodir/psoc-edge-package.zip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:51
msgid "Multiple connected devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:53
msgid ""
"If you have multiple PSOC™ Edge boards connected to your computer, you "
"can identify them by their serial number and flash each one individually."
" To do so, use the ``-n`` flag to provide the serial number of the target"
" board as shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/installation.rst:57
msgid ""
"$ python mp-ifx-flash.py from-package --board KIT_PSE84_AI --zip-package "
"pathtodir/psoc-edge-package.zip -n 181F0D5A01212300"
msgstr ""

