#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:145
msgid "The following parameters have port-specific behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:147
msgid ""
"``priority``: Priority values range from 7 (lowest) to 0 (highest). "
"Default is 7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:151
msgid ""
"All pins on the same port share the same interrupt line. Therefore, only "
"one priority can be set for all pins on the same port. If multiple pins "
"configure interrupts for the same port, the highest priority will be "
"used. If only one pin is configured for an interrupt, its priority can be"
" reconfigured to any value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:157
msgid "The following ``irq()`` features are not supported in this port:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:159
msgid ""
"``trigger``: The ``Pin.IRQ_LOW_LEVEL`` and ``Pin.IRQ_HIGH_LEVEL`` "
"triggers are not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:160
msgid "``wake``: The wake parameter is currently not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:161
msgid ""
"``hard``: This parameter is ignored. It can be passed but currently has "
"no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:165
msgid ""
"**None** of the non-core methods from the Pin API are currently "
"implemented for this port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:169
msgid "Real time clock (RTC)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:171
msgid "See :ref:`machine.RTC <machine.RTC>`: ::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:173
msgid ""
"from machine import RTC\n"
"import time\n"
"\n"
"irq_counter = 0\n"
"\n"
"def cback(event):\n"
"    global irq_counter\n"
"    irq_counter += 1\n"
"\n"
"rtc = RTC()\n"
"rtc.init((2023, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)) # initialise rtc with specific date"
" and time,\n"
"                                      # eg. 2023/1/1 00:00:00\n"
"rtc.datetime((2017, 8, 23, 2, 12, 48, 0, 0)) # set a specific date and\n"
"                                             # time, eg. 2017/8/23 "
"1:12:48\n"
"rtc.datetime() # get date and time\n"
"\n"
"rtc.irq(trigger=RTC.ALARM0, handler=cback)\n"
"rtc.alarm(1000, repeat=False) # set one-shot short alarm in ms\n"
"rtc.alarm_left() # Read the time left for the alarm to expire\n"
"time.sleep_ms(1008) # wait sufficient time\n"
"print(irq_counter) # Check irq counter\n"
"\n"
"rtc.irq(trigger=RTC.ALARM0, handler=cback)\n"
"rtc.alarm(3000, repeat=True) # set periodic short alarm in ms\n"
"rtc.cancel() # cancel the alarm\n"
"\n"
"rtc.irq(trigger=RTC.ALARM0, handler=cback)\n"
"rtc.alarm((2023, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0), repeat=False) # set one-shot "
"longer duration alarm\n"
"\n"
"rtc.memory(b\"hello\") # write bytes into RTC user memory\n"
"rtc.memory() # read bytes from RTC user memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:207
msgid ""
"Setting a random week day in 'wday' field is not valid. The underlying "
"library implements the logic to always calculate the right weekday based "
"on the year, date and month passed. However, datetime() will not raise an"
" error for this but rather re-write the field with the last calculated "
"actual value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:212
msgid "RTC API behavior on this port has the following specifics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:214
msgid ""
"``RTC()`` is a singleton constructor with no ``id`` or additional "
"constructor arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:215
msgid ""
"``rtc.irq()`` accepts alarm trigger ``0`` (``RTC.ALARM0``); ``wake`` is "
"not implemented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:216
msgid ""
"``rtc.alarm()`` accepts ``time`` and optional ``repeat``; no positional "
"alarm ``id`` argument is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:217
msgid ""
"Input ``weekday`` in datetime tuples is ignored and hardware computes the"
" weekday from date fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:218
msgid ""
"The current ``rtc.memory([data])`` maximum payload on KIT_PSE84_AI is 28 "
"bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../psoc-edge/quickref.rst:221
msgid ""
"RTC alarm timing on this port has second-level resolution. Millisecond "
"alarm values are accepted, but are rounded up to whole seconds "
"internally."
msgstr ""

